<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 57,635 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 57,635 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 57,635 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Monday compared to 51,439 tonnes in the same period on Sunday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Monday	December 1</p>
<p>    Export cargo		11,389	18,227</p>
<p>    Import cargo		46,246	33,212</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ships sailed and seven berthed. In the next 24 hours, four are expected to sail and eight are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     33,400	 Marine Hawk	   2/12</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 23,000	 Jaguar		  3/12</p>
<p>Containers		  550	 CMB Antwerp	   3/12</p>
<p>Kerosene/high speed</p>
<p>diesel		   56,000	 Keefan		  4/12</p>
<p>Lubricating oil	 3,864	 Oriental Iris	 5/12</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
